      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-12452",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\pi ,\\,\\pi \u27e9=\u27e8-1,0,\\pi \\,\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12452.json",
          "file_sha256": "7661219b48d572039943434dd824270e4ab8ba07d787838feb01e049ee2a509d"
        }
